= Per-File and Third-Party Notices =

A source file ported from kmscon or libtsm keeps the copyright notice that
file carried, beside vtium's. A third-party component's notice is added here
with the code or data it covers. Each table that a generator writes into
crates/ is named in a paragraph below, with the source it is made from, and
docs/scripts/notices fails when one is not.

GNU Unifont (crates/vtium-font/data/unifont.hex), the font vtium-font builds
in: version 17.0.03, by Roman Czyborra, Paul Hardy and the Unifont
contributors, dual-licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 and the GNU
GPL 2 or later with the GNU font embedding exception. vtium takes it under the
SIL Open Font License 1.1, whose text is crates/vtium-font/data/OFL-1.1.txt in
vtium's source. An installed vtium console carries the same text as
OFL-1.1.txt beside this file.

The geometry of vtium-font's sprites (crates/vtium-font/src/sprite.rs) is
adapted from Ghostty's sprite font, by way of the C fork's font_box.c, under
the MIT licence: Copyright (c) 2024 Mitchell Hashimoto, Ghostty contributors.
The file carries the notice. The table of the kitty placeholder's diacritics,
DIACRITICS in crates/vtium-term/src/placeholder.rs, is copied entry for entry
from Ghostty's src/terminal/kitty/graphics_unicode.zig at commit 0b1729e945,
under the same MIT license and notice, which that file carries too.

X11's color names (crates/vtium-term/src/terminal/color/names.rs and
crates/vtium-term/src/terminal/color/rgb.txt), the table OSC color strings
read names from: the rgb.txt of X.Org's rgb-1.1.1, Copyright 1985, 1989, 1998
The Open Group and Copyright (c) 1994, 2008, Oracle and/or its affiliates,
under the MIT-style licences whose text is
crates/vtium-term/gen-color-names/src/rgb-license.txt in vtium's source. An
installed vtium console carries the same text as rgb-license.txt beside this
file. names.rs carries the notice.

The Unicode data tables, built into vtium and vtium-config: tables made from
the Unicode Character Database 18.0.0 and Unicode's emoji data files of the
same version, Copyright © 1991-2026 Unicode, Inc., under the Unicode License
v3, whose text is at the end of this file and in
crates/vtium-term/gen-unicode/src/unicode-license.txt. Each table carries the
notice. There are three tables, and each is written by the generator beside
its crate:
	crates/vtium-term/src/unicode/data.rs, by vtium-term's gen-unicode: each
	codepoint's grapheme cluster break property, cell width and emoji
	properties.
	crates/vtium/src/deferred/data.rs, by vtium's gen-lookup: the combining
	marks, canonical combining classes, compositions and decompositions that
	the console reads when it looks up a cluster's glyph.
	crates/vtium-config/src/shaping/data.rs, by vtium-config's gen-shaping:
	the emoji sequences, the letters that join to their neighbors and the
	script ranges that vtium-config's shaping reads.

The tests' Unicode data, crates/vtium-term/src/unicode/grapheme_break_test.txt
and crates/vtium-term/src/unicode/above_marks.txt beside it: lists that
vtium-term's gen-unicode makes from GraphemeBreakTest.txt and UnicodeData.txt
of the Unicode Character Database 18.0.0, under the Unicode License v3. Each
list carries the notice. The tests read them; vtium installs none of them.

vtium-config's named cover= sets (crates/vtium-config/src/cover.rs), built
into vtium-config: for each of GB2312, GBK, Big5, JIS X 0208 and KS X 1001,
the codepoints that Unicode's mapping file for that character set maps to.
tools/cover-tables writes the table, and its provenance.tsv names each
mapping file's address, version and SHA-256. The table keeps which codepoints
each file maps to, and none of the mappings. The mapping files are
published by Unicode, Inc., which dates them 1999 to 2015; CP936.TXT,
Microsoft's table, carries no notice of its own. Unicode's terms of use place
each of its data files under the Unicode License v3 unless the file states
terms of its own. The files for GB2312 and KS X 1001 state Unicode's earlier
notice, which grants the right to use the information in them to make
products that support the Unicode Standard.

vtium's terminfo tables (crates/vtium/src/termcap/table.rs), built into
vtium: the capabilities of crates/vtium/install/xterm-vtium.ti, vtium's own
entry, and of crates/vtium/install/kmscon.ti, the C reference's entry, which
a test in crates/vtium/src/termcap.rs writes into the table. They come under
vtium's and kmscon's notices above and need no other.

DejaVu Sans Mono's subsets, the test fixtures
crates/vtium-config/tests/fixtures/DejaVuSansMono-W-M-0.ttf,
DejaVuSansMono-lam-shadda-fatha.ttf and DejaVuSansMono-ascii.ttf beside it:
subsets of DejaVu Sans Mono 2.37, whose glyphs are Copyright (c) 2003 by
Bitstream, Inc. under the Bitstream Vera Fonts licence, with DejaVu's changes
in the public domain. The licence's text is
crates/vtium-config/tests/fixtures/DejaVuSansMono-LICENSE.txt, and the
fixtures' README says how each subset was made. The tests read them; vtium
installs none of them.

Noto Naskh Arabic's subset, the test fixture
crates/vtium-config/tests/fixtures/NotoNaskhArabic-beh-fatha.ttf: a subset of
Noto Naskh Arabic 2.021, Copyright 2022 The Noto Project Authors, under the SIL
Open Font License 1.1. The licence's text is
crates/vtium-config/tests/fixtures/NotoNaskhArabic-LICENSE.txt, and the
fixtures' README says how the subset was made. The tests read it; vtium
installs none of it.

